{
  "id": "VA-HB-1337-2013",
  "scope": "state:va",
  "title": "HB 1337 (2013 Regular Session (LIS session code 131)): Polling place procedures; voter identification to be current, valid, and contain photograph.",
  "urls": [
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?131+sum+HB1337",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?131+mbr+HB1337",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?131+ful+HB1337ER",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?131+ful+CHAP0703 (chapter text; not read)",
    "https://legacylis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?131+ful+HB1337H1 (House committee substitute; not read)"
  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) § 24.2-643 B (as passed (enrolled; struck words removed, new words kept))\n(quote) The officer shall ask the voter to present any one of the following forms of identification: his Commonwealth of Virginia voter registration card; his Virginia driver's license; his concealed handgun permit issued pursuant to § 18.2-308; any other identification card issued by a government agency of the Commonwealth, one of its political subdivisions, or the United States; any student identification card issued by any institution of higher education located in the Commonwealth of Virginia; or any employee identification card issued by an employer of the voter in the ordinary course of the employer's business. All forms of identification permitted in this subsection are required to (i) be current and valid and (ii) contain a photograph or the name and address of the voter.\n(b_no_id_remedy)\n(section) § 24.2-643 B, second paragraph (existing text reprinted, unchanged)\n(quote) Any voter who does not show one of the forms of identification specified in this subsection shall be offered a provisional ballot under the provisions of § 24.2-653. The State Board of Elections shall provide an ID-ONLY provisional ballot envelope that requires no follow-up action by the registrar or electoral board other than matching submitted identification documents from the voter for the electoral board to make a determination on whether to count the ballot.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) Enactment clause 2 (as passed)\n(quote) 2. That the provisions of this act shall become effective on July 1, 2014, provided an appropriation providing for a voter outreach or public information program and otherwise effectuating the purposes of this act is included in a general appropriation act passed during the 2014 Regular Session of the General Assembly that becomes law.\n(other) § 24.2-701 C: absentee application contents (rank/grade/service number, religion, workplace address, designating party chairman or candidate)",
  "sponsors": [
    {
      "name": "Mark L. Cole",
      "role": "author",
      "version": "Chaptered: Acts of Assembly Chapter 703, approved 3/23/2013 (text read as enrolled HB1337ER, 2/22/2013, after Senate amendment)"
    }
  ],
